### Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server

This SDK is also an installable MCP server where the various SDK methods are
exposed as tools that can be invoked by AI applications.

> Node.js v20 or greater is required to run the MCP server from npm.

<details>
<summary>Claude installation steps</summary>

Add the following server definition to your `claude_desktop_config.json` file:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{sanitizeClassName .Global.AST.MainSDK.Type.Name}}": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y", "--package", "{{.Global.Config.PackageName}}",
        "--",
        "mcp", "start"
        {{- if gt (len $flags) 0 }},
        {{-   range $i, $entry := $flags }}
        "{{$entry.key}}", "{{$entry.value}}"{{if lt (add $i 1) (len $flags)}},{{end}}
        {{-   end }}
        {{- end }}
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

</details>

<details>
<summary>Cursor installation steps</summary>

Create a `.cursor/mcp.json` file in your project root with the following content:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{sanitizeClassName .Global.AST.MainSDK.Type.Name}}": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y", "--package", "{{.Global.Config.PackageName}}",
        "--",
        "mcp", "start"
        {{- if gt (len $flags) 0 }},
        {{-   range $i, $entry := $flags }}
        "{{$entry.key}}", "{{$entry.value}}"{{if lt (add $i 1) (len $flags)}},{{end}}
        {{-   end }}
        {{- end }}
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

</details>

You can also run MCP servers as a standalone binary with no additional dependencies. You must pull these binaries from available Github releases:

```bash
curl -L -o mcp-server \
    https://github.com/{org}/{repo}/releases/download/{tag}/mcp-server-bun-darwin-arm64 && \
chmod +x mcp-server
```

If the repo is a private repo you must add your Github PAT to download a release `-H "Authorization: Bearer {GITHUB_PAT}"`.


```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "Todos": {
      "command": "./DOWNLOAD/PATH/mcp-server",
      "args": [
        "start"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

For a full list of server arguments, run:

```sh
npx -y --package {{.Global.Config.PackageName}} -- mcp start --help
```
{{- end }}{{/* if and .Global.Config.Published isMCPServerEnabled */}}